  "note": "Seventh contract set on Robinhood Chain mainnet, planned: the protocol moves from BRSR to $BURSAR, the token the operator launched on Pons. Everything that holds the staked token is new, because none of it can be pointed at another token: the staking pool, the buyback, the credit pool and collateral vault built on them, and the dispute layer around the resolver registry, which takes a new escrow, reputation and mandate factory with it, the committed-mandate contracts that lock on that escrow, and the treasury park with its two adapters, which admits mandates from one factory fixed at construction. Buybacks are off: the buyback is deployed only because the credit pool prices a write-off at its ceiling, has no keeper, is paused by the wiring batch and is never funded. The 48-hour timelock, the agent registry, the asset registry, price guard and stock router, the shielded pool and the endowments carry over from rhc-mainnet-v6 at their addresses. Mandates on the sixth escrow keep working there and are not moved. Each deploy script writes its own section as it runs. The status turns live when the apps move to this set, and rhc-mainnet-v6 retires once nothing is open on its escrow, registries, credit pool and vault.",
